  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\left|z-\\frac{4}{z}\\right|=2$, then the maximum value of $|z|$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "boZH0",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{3}+1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IigIL",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{5}+1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Hcnag",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HlmMB",
      "text": "\n$2+\\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& |z|=\\left|\\left(z-\\frac{4}{z}\\right)+\\frac{4}{z}\\right| \\Rightarrow|z|=\\left|z-\\frac{4}{z}+\\frac{4}{z}\\right| \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow|z| \\leq\\left|z-\\frac{4}{z}\\right|+\\frac{4}{|z|} \\Rightarrow|z| \\leq 2+\\frac{4}{|z|}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow|z|^2-2|z|-4 \\leq 0 \\\\\n& (|z|-(\\sqrt{5}+1))(|z|-(1-\\sqrt{5})) \\leq 0 \\Rightarrow 1-\\sqrt{5} \\leq|z| \\leq \\sqrt{5}+1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
